What is Flutter?
Interview answer

Flutter is an open-source UI framework by Google used to build cross-platform applications from a single codebase.

It uses Dart as its programming language and provides its own widget-based UI system.

You can use Flutter to build:

Android apps
iOS apps
Web apps
Desktop applications
Simple way to remember

Flutter = framework
Dart = programming language
Widget = basic building block of Flutter UI

Interview follow-up

Q: Why can Flutter build Android and iOS apps from one codebase?

Because Flutter provides a cross-platform framework and rendering system, allowing the same Dart/Flutter codebase to be used across different platforms, with platform-specific functionality accessed when needed.